# Mode two: the Elvish Mystic gets a +1/+1 counter first (making it 2/2) and then deals damage equal to its power, 2, to
# Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2), which dies: without the counter the Mystic's 1 damage would not kill it, so this proves the
# power is read after the counter. One-sided: the Mystic takes no damage in return (unlike a fight).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Elvish Mystic
Archdruid's Charm
Plains x3
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Archdruid's Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
Bot1.Target(Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic.Damage = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Stack.Count = 0
